 "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pits Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy, with Libertarian Donald Kissick also on the ballot. October polls consistently put Acton in front, with most mid-October surveys showing her leading by two to eight points and the aggregated margin near four points. Prediction markets have moved sharply in her direction, pricing her win chances around 80 to 85 percent.\n\nThe race was upended in late October by a Ramaswamy attack ad featuring Acton's estranged mother, which drew broad criticism and a public defense from Trump. Ramaswamy retains real advantages: a Republican-leaning state, a large fundraising and cash edge, and fundamentals that slightly favor Republicans. Expert raters mostly call the race a Tossup, with a few moving to Lean or Likely Democratic. The forecast expects a narrow Acton lead with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6672, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6954, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6809, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7082, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7607, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7343, "margin": 3.5